### Summary of behavior implemented

| Requirement | How it's met |
|---|---|
| Fixed substring (not regex) | `memcmp` scan in `line_matches` |
| Empty pattern matches every line | `pattern_len == 0 → return 1` |
| Case-sensitive | `memcmp` is byte-exact |
| `--` ends option parsing | `options_done` flag |
| Unsupported option → usage + exit 2 | Checked before pattern is set |
| No PATTERN → usage + exit 2 | `pattern == NULL` check after loop |
| `-` is an ordinary filename | Only `-` with length > 1 triggers option check |
| No files → search stdin | `nfiles == 0` branch |
| Files → never read stdin | `nfiles > 0` branch only opens files |
| One file → no prefix; two+ → `operand:` | `use_prefix = (nfiles >= 2)` |
| Follow symlinks | `stat()` follows symlinks by default |
| Directory/missing/unreadable → diagnose, continue | `stat`/`fopen` error paths with `continue` |
| Exit 0/1/2 semantics | `overall_match`/`overall_error` at the end |
| stderr empty on success | No `fprintf(stderr,…)` on the happy path |
| Arbitrary bytes (NUL, CR, invalid UTF-8) | `unsigned char` buffers, byte-level `memcmp` |
| Final unterminated line is a line | Handled after the read loop |
| Every selected line emitted once with newline | Single emission per line, `fputc('\n')` |
| Empty input emits nothing | Loop exits immediately, `line_len == 0` |
| Long lines without crash | Growable buffer with `SIZE_MAX/2` overflow guard |
| Allocation/read/write failure handled | `had_error` flag, no UB |
| `search_stream` semantic anchor | Named function called from `main` |
| No external utilities | Only libc/POSIX calls |
| C11 + POSIX.1-2008 | Compiles with the specified flags |

